  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Samoa-Australia Policing Partnership (SAPP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SAPP leads and coordinates AFP engagement with the Samoa Police, Prisons and Corrections Service (SPPCS). The SAPP provides the framework for collaboration between the SPPCS and AFP to strengthen SPPCS&#x2019; delivery of its mandate to maintain a safe and stable Samoa. The SAPP 2021-25 design came into effect July 2021 and is framed by the following Partnership Goal: to support SPPCS to maintain a safe and stable Samoa. Two Partnership Outcomes support this goal: SPPCS has the workforce and institutional capacity to deliver high quality corporate and strategic planning and management; and SPPCS has enhanced capabilities in targeted areas aligned to both the Samoa Law and Justice Sector Plan (2012-2016) and AFP International Engagement Strategies and Plans.</narrative>
  </description>
